{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115858",
      "title": "Understanding Directives",
      "lectureOrder": 151,
      "videoOrder": 143,
      "sourceHash": "5cffed8ca5bcb2c679a86122164f10c8e480c15585dabd6644f44733bb288e9a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.81,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "So what are Directives?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 7.32,
          "en": "Well, Directives, in the end, are enhancements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.32,
          "end": 10.41,
          "en": "for elements you're using in your templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.41,
          "end": 12.278,
          "en": "No matter if we're talking about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.278,
          "end": 16.32,
          "en": "standard built-in HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.32,
          "end": 19.29,
          "en": "or about Angular components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.29,
          "end": 23.04,
          "en": "both types of elements can be enhanced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.04,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "with help of Directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 29.19,
          "en": "And enhance means that extra behaviors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 33.543,
          "en": "or settings can be added to those elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 36.39,
          "en": "For example, you could use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.39,
          "end": 39.48,
          "en": "the built-in NgModel directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.48,
          "end": 42.33,
          "en": "which you did already see in action earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.33,
          "end": 45.12,
          "en": "in the course with two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.12,
          "end": 48.821,
          "en": "You can add that on an input to make Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.821,
          "end": 51.09,
          "en": "aware of that input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "You could, for example, then use it with two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 57.12,
          "en": "to read the input value and set it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.12,
          "end": 59.459,
          "en": "but you can also use it without two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.459,
          "end": 63,
          "en": "though you'll learn more about that later in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63,
          "end": 64.92,
          "en": "in the forms section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.92,
          "end": 69.36,
          "en": "The main takeaway is that NgModel here would be a Directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.36,
          "end": 70.98,
          "en": "It's not a Component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 74.55,
          "en": "Instead, it's just there to, under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 77.46000000000001,
          "en": "enhance the input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.46000000000001,
          "end": 79.578,
          "en": "for example, with two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.578,
          "end": 81.78,
          "en": "or in other ways about which you will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.78,
          "end": 83.253,
          "en": "learn later in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.3,
          "end": 87.06,
          "en": "So that's the idea behind Directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.06,
          "end": 91.68,
          "en": "And unlike Components, Directives have no template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.68,
          "end": 92.98400000000001,
          "en": "because other than that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.98400000000001,
          "end": 94.785,
          "en": "they're essentially the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.785,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "because in the end, Components are Directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 101.28,
          "en": "but Directives with a template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.28,
          "end": 105.63,
          "en": "because Components, of course, also enhance elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.63,
          "end": 108.3,
          "en": "They enhance the element you are selecting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.3,
          "end": 110.52000000000001,
          "en": "with the Component selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 112.25999999999999,
          "en": "That can, in the end, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.25999999999999,
          "end": 116.1,
          "en": "lead to pretty much a brand new element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.1,
          "end": 119.64,
          "en": "being available if you're using the tag selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.64,
          "end": 121.23,
          "en": "But earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.23,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "you saw examples where we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 128.19,
          "en": "also selected a button which had a specific attribute on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.19,
          "end": 129.93,
          "en": "and we then enhanced that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.93,
          "end": 134.58,
          "en": "But we did that by also changing the markup of that button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.58,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "by adding a template to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 139.47,
          "en": "to change what's rendered between the button tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "And that's what Components are all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "They enhance elements also by bringing their own template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 149.7,
          "en": "which will then be rendered onto the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.7,
          "end": 152.04,
          "en": "Directives are almost like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.04,
          "end": 154.32,
          "en": "but they don't have their own template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.32,
          "end": 157.66899999999998,
          "en": "Instead, they're just there to enhance the properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.66899999999998,
          "end": 161.31,
          "en": "attributes, or behaviors of elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.31,
          "end": 163.653,
          "en": "but they do not bring a template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 167.13,
          "en": "That's what Directives are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "but that's, of course, just the theory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "Let's now take a look at Directives in practice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 175.383,
          "en": "in action to get a better feeling for them.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
